@startuml qnx_dispatch_engine_unselect_endpoint_activity
title QnxDispatchEngine - client endpoint removal

start
:Enter UnselectEndpoint(endpoint);
:Find a poll slot holding this endpoint pointer;
if (A matching slot exists?) then (yes)
    :Save its index and nonce\nSet the slot endpoint to nullptr;
    :Iterate the new-data and ping signal values;
    while (Another signal?) is (yes)
        :Rebuild the event from the saved index/nonce,\nsignal, client side channel and kSelectPulseCode;
        :MsgUnregisterEvent(event)\nIgnore its result;
    endwhile (no)
else (not found)
    :Skip native event unregistration;
endif
if (endpoint.disconnect is non-empty?) then (yes)
    :Invoke endpoint.disconnect() in this caller's context;
else (empty)
    :Skip the disconnect callback;
endif
:Return from the helper;
stop

legend
    Public UnregisterPosixEndpoint asserts engine callback context,
    erases the intrusive-list entry, then invokes this helper.
    ProcessCleanup also invokes this helper for matching-owner entries.
    List removal belongs to those callers, not this helper.
    The nonce is retained on removal and incremented on slot reuse.
    A missing poll slot does not suppress a non-empty disconnect callback.
    Any descriptor closure belongs to consumer/callback policy.
endlegend

@enduml
